    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "A school invests $\\$5000$ at the end of each year at 6% p.a. to go towards a new library.\nHow much will the school have after 10 years? Give your answer to the nearest cent.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$65\\,903.97$",
      "worked": "End of 1st year: $5000$\n\nEnd of 2nd year: $5000(1.06)+5000$\n\nEnd of 10th year: $5000(1.06)^9+5000(1.06)^8+\\cdots+5000$\n\nThis is a geometric series with $a=5000$, common ratio $R=1.06$ and $n=10$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}FV&=\\frac{a(R^{n}-1)}{R-1}\\\\FV&=\\frac{5000(1.06^{10}-1)}{1.06-1}\\\\FV&\\approx\\$65\\,903.97\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
